# Client-Facing Handling

Per the reference methodology, the sheet list and count tables are held
internal. The client narrative states the sheet total, the MEP split, and the
documentation approach — nothing lower.

The reasoning is commercial: these tables are the estimating basis. Publishing
them before the design exists invites line-item negotiation against sheets that
have not been drawn.

What the client narrative may state:

- Approximately PLACEHOLDER sheets, firming on receipt of the DD set
- PLACEHOLDER: MEP split and who holds the general and architectural series
- Signed and sealed by PLACEHOLDER Virginia PEs
- PLACEHOLDER: specification approach

What it must not state: per-sheet enumeration, the low/high range, or the range
drivers.

